abstract: >
  Triadic Reality Theory proposes that determinate actuality requires three
  irreducible co-primitives: L3 as ontological logical constraint, I-infinity as
  unbounded informational representability/differentiation, and A as fundamental
  state transition/change. Representability, L3-admissibility, actualizability,
  and actuality are kept distinct.
